      "prompt": "Convert $y={{a}}(x{{nh|signed}})^2{{k|signed}}$ to COMPLETE standard form $y=ax^2+bx+c$.",
      "responseFields": [
        {
          "id": "answer",
          "label": "Standard-form equation",
          "inputProfile": "equation",
          "expected": "y={{a}}x^2{{bcoef|signed}}x{{ccoef|signed}}"
        }
      ],
      "solutionReview": {
        "headline": "Conversion means expanding the entire square and combining every term.",
        "reasoning": [
          "$(x-h)^2=x^2-2hx+h^2$; multiplying by {{a}} gives the quadratic and linear coefficients.",
          "After adding {{k}}, the standard form is $y={{a}}x^2{{bcoef|signed}}x{{ccoef|signed}}$."
        ]
      },
      "attemptFeedback": [
        "A complete conversion needs the $x^2$ term, x term, and constant—not just one coefficient."
      ],
      "supportHints": [
        "Expand the binomial square before multiplying by a."
      ],
